here are the best viral products i  tested in 2021.  let's start with brows the huda beauty  bomb brows micro shade brow pencil has  this incredibly thin point that makes it  so easy to make hair like strokes it is  a little fragile so be careful with how  much pressure you're using but i love  this pencil if you struggle with using  pencils to fill in your brows i highly  recommend this mad love brow stamp kit  you apply one of the stencils to your  brow and stamp the brow color onto fill  it makes doing your brows so fast and  easy and you don't have to worry about  having two different brow shapes now my  favorite brow setting products everyone  went nuts for the abh brow freeze and so  did i it gives your brows that fluffy  laminated look and keeps the hair locked  in place all day but i recently tried  the elf brow lift and i swear it works  exactly the same it also came out with  this special applicator that really lets  you press those hairs down moving on to  complexion products the fenty beauty  ease drop blurring skin tint is so  natural and beautiful on the skin the  coverage is minimal but very buildable  the l'oreal true match nude hyaluronic  tinted serum is another great option it  evens out the skin and gives you a very  glowy hydrated finish plus you get the  added benefits of hyaluronic acid  the pseudolabs freckles kit is  definitely the best product i've ever  used for creating faux freckles you use  the freckle liquid which has this little  round brush in it and this little  toothpick looking thing to flick the  liquid onto your face and it gives you  these very natural looking freckles this  givenchy prisma libre loose powder is a  huge splurge item that actually lived up  to the hype the colors all blend into  one translucent shade that really  brightens up the under eyes and sets the  face without leaving you feeling dry it  makes the skin look so smooth next my  favorite makeup product blush i tried so  many different kinds this year i think  my favorite was definitely the melt  cosmetics cream blush light this formula  is pigmented and blended like a dream it  layered over powder really really nicely  the m cosmetics so soft blush is also a  cream blush but in a stick form this one  is very user friendly because it is so  soft and easy to blend out you don't  have to worry about overdoing it the  made by mitchell blursh liquid blusher  is probably the best liquid blush  formula i've ever tried i applied this  over my already set foundation and it's  still blended out so well without  removing any product underneath and the  pigment is so intense  now onto bronzer just like the blush m  cosmetics so soft multi face play is  creamy and easy to use the shade i got  was more of a contour color for me but  there are some warmer shades for  bronzing the elf putty bronzer is  another amazing bronzer and an  affordable one the blendability of this  bronzer is unreal it has this really  interesting formula that goes from a  cream to more of a powder finish it's so  easy to work with  next we have some really interesting eye  products these chameleon flakes from  kyma cosmetics are like little shavings  of pigment that shift color they  definitely have a bit of a learning  curve but once you get it they look  amazing on the eyes this product is  technically a multi-use product but i'm  putting it here this is the janessa  myrick's beauty color fix eye cheek and  lip cream pigment the pigment in these  is no joke a little goes such a long way  and the fact that you can use them as so  many different things under eye  corrector blush eyeliner lipstick  eyeshadow is definitely a plus  and finally a few of the best lip  products i tried if you want that full  coverage transfer proof lip definitely  check out the nyx lip lingerie xxl matte  liquid lipsticks one thin layer is all  you need and once they dry down they're  not moving the milani color fetish matte  lipstick is also very pigmented and  wears really nicely these aren't as  matte as you would think and they still  have that comfortable slip that you'd  get from a regular lipstick  [Music]
 

